    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The acceptance tests are the only test classes, and both pass with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented soft-delete for owners across the Spring Boot app:\n\n**Domain model** (`Owner.java`)\n- Added a `deleted` boolean field (`@Column(name = \"deleted\", nullable = false)`) initialized to `false`, with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted(...)` accessors. A newly created owner is therefore `false` by default.\n\n**API contract** (`openapi.yml`)\n- Added a read-only `deleted` boolean property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps it automatically \u2014 `GET /api/owners/{id}` now returns `deleted`.\n\n**Controller** (`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`)\n- `deleteOwner` now marks the owner (`setDeleted(true)`) and saves it instead of removing the row, still returning `204 No Content` (2xx). The record is retained, so `GET` keeps returning it.\n- `requireUniqueIdentity` and `requireNoHouseholdDuplicate` now filter out `deleted` owners, so a normally-blocking duplicate/identity match is allowed when the only matching owner has been soft-deleted.\n\n**Schema** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`)\n- Added the `deleted` column with a `DEFAULT FALSE`/`DEFAULT 0` `NOT NULL` so existing seed inserts (which don't list the column) default to not-deleted.\n\nBoth acceptance tests \u2014 `coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains` (flag flips false\u2192true, record retained) and `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck` (recreating a deleted owner's payload is allowed) \u2014 pass, with the full suite green.\n\nOne scoping note: I limited the \"ignore deleted\" change to the two blocking checks the spec calls out (duplicate and identity). The soft signals (possible-duplicate flag, namesake count, customer-code de-duplication, city/day capacity) still consider deleted rows; they're non-blocking and the spec only required the duplicate/identity checks to change. Happy to extend to those too if you'd prefer deleted owners be fully invisible to create.",
